course: dictionary
lesson: 3018
title: Dying: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one you need. «Dying» can mean coming to the end of life. It can also mean fading or ending, as in «a dying fire». In everyday talk it can mean wanting something very much, as in «I'm dying to know».
explain: Read the clues. In «The fire was dying, so we added a log», the fire is not a living thing that is about to die. It is losing its flames and going out. Nobody is really about to die when someone says «I'm dying for a drink»: it is an exaggeration that means they want a drink very much.
explain: Some uses are very serious. In stories, history and real life, dying describes death and loss, so choose your words with care. Jaz from Yorkshire groans, «This box weighs a ton, I'm literally dying, our kid». He is only tired, and a pulley could help him lift the box.
fact: Dying can mean coming to the end of life, or being about to die.
fact: Dying can also mean fading or ending, like «a dying fire» or «a dying light».
fact: «Dying to» or «dying for» means wanting something very much. It is informal, so keep it for chatty talk, not serious writing.
fact: «A dying wish» is someone's last wish, and «a dying breed» is something that is becoming rare.
fact: Plants dying without water or light show that living things need these things to stay alive.
exercise: «The fire was dying, so we added a log.» What does dying mean here? | Singing happily | Growing bigger and hotter | Being very hungry | *Fading and going out
exercise: Jaz says, «I'm dying for a drink.» Does he mean he is about to die? | Yes, he is about to die of thirst | Yes, he is dying of a cold | He is very cold and wet | *No, he means he wants a drink very much
exercise: «Many families take turns to sit with a dying relative so that they are never alone.» What does dying mean here? | Fading like a fire | Wanting something very much | Tired after a long walk | *Coming to the end of life
test: Why should you check big news about a famous person dying on a trusted news website? | Because famous people never die | *Because fake death stories spread a lot online | Because it costs nothing to share | Because news websites are always boring
test: What does «a dying wish» mean? | *Someone's last wish, near the end of life | A wish to be very hungry | A wish for a new bike | A wish that is always granted
exam: Jaz says, «I'm literally dying» about a heavy box. What does this tell you? | He is dying to meet his brother | He is really about to die | *He is exaggerating, because he is only tired | He is dying of hunger
